## Teardown
docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 down -v --rmi all
docker image prune -f
Result: All 4 images (3 Cacti + 1 MariaDB) removed, volumes cleaned, network removed.

## Architecture Notes
- Real Cacti from git clone at each release tag (NOT copied/lifted)
- Real MariaDB 10.6 (per-version instance, tmpfs for speed)
- pcb_probe.php includes REAL lib/api_automation.php from the Cacti installation
  - build_matching_objects_filter() and build_rule_item_filter() run from their original location
  - api_automation_column_exists() (V1+) runs from its original location
  - db_column_exists() queries the REAL MariaDB schema
- External HTTP trigger: GET /pcb_probe.php?action=run&... over TCP to Apache
- Authentication context: Cacti's auth mechanism is present; probe bypasses session but uses the same DB functions (the CVE requires admin auth which is a precondition, not part of the differential)
